{"id": "sllama0139", "pool": "sllama", "arm": "aggressive", "tier": "aggressive", "lang": "en", "run_id": "ttfa1", "attempt": 1, "seed": 3934765946, "protocol": "ttfa-v3", "config_sha256": "25e6887f8551649e559d24b54bbd2fe07f238cfc4d1ce1fc5ff87b67005b2d8d", "gate_art_sha256": "0e6494c2eeac9bcd86c10b5def3cbd32e98bb0765fa2fd8afc8c1b47915ea372", "threshold": 0.5533501505851746, "gpu": "NVIDIA H100 80GB HBM3", "host": "modal", "shard": 5, "query": "What is the slowest moving animal? ", "input_path": "/data/bench_audio/sllama0139.wav", "input_sha256": "b24f2a9e1aedc72d212beb70bc69eae27fba5fab8cccfb1a607ff96af0c60925", "input_samples": 39584, "input_s": 2.474, "n_real_chunks": 3, "score": 0.7254, "act": 0.9976, "is_info": true, "fired": true, "mode": "escalated", "answer": "", "relay_text": "The slowest-moving animal is generally considered the three-toed sloth, which moves at about 0.24 km/h or 0.15 mph on land. If including very small or unusual animals, some creatures like snails or sea anemones can move even more slowly, but the three-toed sloth is the standard answer.", "expert_answer": "The **slowest-moving animal is generally considered the three-toed sloth**, which moves at about **0.24 km/h** or **0.15 mph** on land.\n\nIf including very small or unusual animals, some creatures like **snails** or **sea anemones** can move even more slowly, but the **three-toed sloth** is the standard answer.", "transcript": "What is the slowest moving animal?\n", "asr_s": 0.93, "expert_s": 3.27, "expert_input_samples": 39584, "expert_input_s": 2.474, "expert_input_sha256": "b24f2a9e1aedc72d212beb70bc69eae27fba5fab8cccfb1a607ff96af0c60925", "expert_timed_out": false, "wait_s": 3.355, "relay_synth_ms": 9725, "onset_chunk": 3, "eot_seen": false, "n_speak_chunks": 1, "feed_lag_max_ms": 43, "feed_lag_sum_ms": 43, "audio_files": {"relay": {"path": "/data/ttfa_real/ttfa1/sllama/audio/sllama0139_aggressive_relay.wav", "sha256": "c2f4718c965cd837d60aec375780655c360dc0e37127ecf1b37118dc027e